>> title: White Cut Chicken
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: chicken, chinese, poached, cold plate, ginger
>> counters: Dim Sum Counter
>> aka: bak chit gai, baak cit gai, 白切雞, white cooked chicken, poached chicken, plain chicken
>> pairs-with: ginger-scallion-oil
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr 30 min
>> step.1: poach 30 min off the heat, lid on
>> step.2: chill in an ice bath 15 min, until the skin draws tight
>> step.3: rest 20 min, rub with sesame oil, chop

Poach @whole chicken{3 1/2%lb}(1.6 kg) breast-down in a #stockpot{} of @water{4%qt}(3.8 L) brought to the boil with @fresh ginger{6%slices}(coin-sized), @scallions{3}(knotted) and @kosher salt{2%Tbs}: bring it back to a tremble, put the lid on, take the pot off the heat altogether and leave it ~poach{30%min}. Boiling shreds the breast and clouds the skin.

Lift @&(~1)chicken{} straight into @iced water{4%qt}(3.8 L; half of it ice) and ~chill{15%min}. The shock is the whole point — it draws the skin tight and sets the layer of fat under it to a jelly.

Drain @&(~1)chicken{}, ~rest{20%min} on a rack, rub it over with @toasted sesame oil{2%tsp}, and chop it through the bone. It is served at room temperature, and it is served with ginger-scallion oil — plain chicken and a bowl of the relish are one dish, not a dish and a sauce.
